-- title:
--   Residues of L(f)-elements lie in k(̄ fᵢ)
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be an algebraically closed field, $A \subseteq L$ a valuation subring with residue field $k =$ `IsLocalRing.ResidueField A`, and $F/L$ a field extension. Let $\iota$ be an index type and, for each $i : \iota$, let $Fb\,i$ be a field equipped with a $k$-algebra structure and let $R\,i$ be a regular prolongation of $A$ to $F$ with residue field $Fb\,i$: that is, a valuation subring $(R\,i).\mathrm{integers}$ of $F$ together with a ring homomorphism $(R\,i).\mathrm{residue}$ from it onto $Fb\,i$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal, such that an element of $L$ lands in $(R\,i).\mathrm{integers}$ exactly when it lies in $A$, the residue map restricted to $A$ is the structure map $k \to Fb\,i$ composed with the residue of $A$, and every nonzero element of $F$ has an $L$-multiple that is integral with nonzero residue. Let $f \in F$ be integral for every $R\,i$, with residue $\overline f_i := (R\,i).\mathrm{residue}\,f$ transcendental over $k$ for every $i$. Then for all indices $i_0, i$ and every $w$ in the intermediate field $L(f) \subseteq F$ generated by $f$ over $L$, assuming $w$ integral for $R\,i_0$ and integral for $R\,i$, the residue $(R\,i).\mathrm{residue}\,w$ lies in the intermediate field of $Fb\,i$ generated over $k$ by $\overline f_i$, i.e. in $k(\overline f_i)$.
--
--   This is one inclusion of the identification of the residue field of the Gauss prolongation $W = (R\,i_0).\mathrm{integers} \cap L(f)$ with the rational function field $k(\overline f_i)$, the Gauss-content normalisation attached to a transcendental residue; the complementary inclusion is the surjectivity of $k(\overline f_i)$ onto the image of $\kappa(W)$. It feeds the construction of Gauss bases and of elements of prescribed valuation used in [`AlgebraicCurve.RegularProlongation.exists_finset_forall_valuation_eq_one_forall_exists_mem_integers_residue_uniqueRepr_and_span`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.RegularProlongation.exists_finset_forall_valuation_eq_one_forall_exists_mem_integers_residue_uniqueRepr_and_span) and [`AlgebraicCurve.RegularProlongation.exists_gaussBasis_mem_integralClosure_piResidue_uniqueRepr_of_sum_finrank_eq`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.RegularProlongation.exists_gaussBasis_mem_integralClosure_piResidue_uniqueRepr_of_sum_finrank_eq).
